  "worked_solution": "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{9}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{3}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+12 & =16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =0,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
